Audio subsystem provenance
===========================

This directory contains a minimal freestanding compatibility layer that lets
the upstream Neo Geo sound CPU run on the Sega Saturn SH-2 target.

Imported code (used under its original open-source terms):
  - audio_saturn.c  : local copy of deps/kof98recomp/neogeorecomp/src/audio.c
  - ng_internal.h   : local copy of deps/kof98recomp/neogeorecomp/src/ng_internal.h
    Source: https://github.com/danilopaulinodasilva/kof98recomp (neogeorecomp).
    Only two mechanical patches are applied (see tools/_make_audio_saturn.py):
    KOF_32BIT_CYCLES-aware ng_cycles type, and an M1->SM1 ROM fallback.

The YM2610 synthesis library (ext/ymfm) and the Z80 core (ext/z80) are NOT
copied here: they are compiled directly from deps/kof98recomp/neogeorecomp/ext.
ymfm is BSD 3-Clause, Copyright (c) 2021 Aaron Giles; its license header is
preserved in the original files.

The remaining headers in this directory (cstdint, cassert, cstring, cstdio,
algorithm, array, memory, string, vector, shim_*) are original minimal
freestanding shims written for this project, because the SH-2 toolchain has no
C++ standard library.
